    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) standing as the clear headliner. His elite sprint speed aligns perfectly with a favorable matchup against Bubba Chandler, and his robust 0.373 xwOBA ensures he remains the primary engine for our category scarcity needs in SB. Joining him at the top of the leaderboard, **Yordan Alvarez** (74.28) and **Trea Turner** (73.97) provide the necessary high-floor stability. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a locked-in start despite a park factor drag, as his 0.443 xwOBA overrides the slight disadvantage against Freddy Peralta. **Trea Turner** rounds out the elite tier, benefiting from a high-leverage #2 spot in the order and a soft matchup against the 4.69 xERA of Gavin Holmes.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the card involved **Chase Meidroth** (49.89), who narrowly missed the cut behind the platoon-heavy upside of **Dillon Dingler** (48.27). While **Chase Meidroth** possesses a solid profile against Michael McGreevy, the optimizer prioritized the specific park-adjusted, SP-skill-derived advantages found in **Dillon Dingler**'s matchup. Additionally, we are monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Caleb Durbin**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Yordan Alvarez**. While their projected scores of 54.68, 67.64, and 74.28 respectively suggest must-start territory, any shift in their batting order\u2014particularly if **Caleb Durbin** drops further down the lineup\u2014could necessitate an immediate recalibration to protect our daily efficiency targets. We are also proceeding with caution regarding **Gary Sanchez** (41.10) and **Carson Benge** (43.39), as both face elite arms in Corbin Burnes and Luke Schlittler, respectively; these players are on the roster fringe today and should be monitored for defensive replacement risks.",
